      "rag": {
        "answer": "The Idempotency\u2011Key header carries a client\u2011generated UUID\u202fv4 that uniquely identifies a payment request. When the gateway receives such a request, it stores the resulting response in Redis for 24\u202fhours. If the same request is sent again (e.g., after a network glitch) with the identical Idempotency\u2011Key, the gateway detects the cached entry, returns it with an **X\u2011Cache\u2011Lookup:\u202fHIT** header, and **does not re\u2011execute the database mutation or credit\u2011card charge**\u3010Source\u202f1\u3011\u3010Source\u202f2\u3011. This ensures that only one charge is processed even if the request is retried.",
        "citations": [
